import Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases

/-!
# Nodes for descent inside the even Ree two Sylow subgroup

This family fixes 600 proposed nodes for maximal-subgroup descent inside the
parity kernel, pruning only noncentric subgroups and subgroups contained in
the core-character kernel. Node zero is the parity kernel. The 59 prescribed
Frattini survivors are retained verbatim by reference to `smallEvenCandidate`.
The other nodes are closures of explicit root words. These definitions assert
no orders, centricity, completeness, or Frattini-action properties.

Source: the root convention of Shinoda (1975), (2.3), pp. 81–82. Diagnostic
labels identify words from the exploratory maximal-subgroup calculation;
all mathematical properties require separate Lean proofs.
-/

namespace ReeTwo.SylowModel

set_option maxRecDepth 10000

